From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Connor McAdams <cmcadams@codeweavers.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Jan 2026 14:00:30 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] d3dx10: Add partial support for saving to DDS files in
 D3DX10SaveTextureToMemory().

Add support for saving DDS files with non-DXT10 DDS headers.

Signed-off-by: Connor McAdams <cmcadams@codeweavers.com>

CW-Bug-Id: #20442
CW-Bug-Id: #23084
CW-Bug-Id: #23301
(cherry picked from commit e3bf5801d01db61bfe03a6612616823be0a16f59)
mproton-resolved: 11.20 replaced Proton's struct d3d10_texture helpers with d3dx_texture_info and the d3d10 staging-resource helpers, so D3DX10SaveTextureToMemory() is rewritten on those: each subresource is copied into a CPU-readable staging texture, mapped, and converted into the DDS image's pixels. The cube-map flag comes from the texture desc (d3dx_texture_info has none). The d3dx9 helper hunks apply as is. Proton's test changes are left out: they edit save tests that the series doesn't carry (batch 1 left them out with the stub commit).
